    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0767" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.796/10–2346</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 2327</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-23">October 23, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        29.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith copy
                    of a memorandum prepared by Commercial Attaché Howard, in which is outlined the
                    present policy and attitude of the Cuban Government authorities concerned <pb
                        facs="0768" n="750" xml:id="pg750"/> with civil aviation matters. The
                    development of this policy has almost in its entirety taken place over the past
                    year and a half and is motivated primarily by a desire to secure to Cuban
                    companies reciprocal privileges from the countries of which foreign airlines
                    operating into Cuba are nationals.</p>
                <p>The data in the enclosed memorandum should be very useful to the Department in
                    the event of bilateral aviation discussions with Cuba. Moreover, I believe that
                    this resume will be of great value to American companies who are considering
                    operations to Cuba, but owing to its nature should be made available with
                    discretion.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Norweb</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d659-a1.xml" xpointer="d659-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
